# ttt model aliases — copy to ~/.config/ttt/models
#
# `alias = model id`, one per line. `ttt load smart`, `ttt unload coder`,
# `ttt say --model tts` all resolve through this file first, then through the
# built-in aliases below, and anything unrecognised is passed through as a
# literal model id — so a full id always works.
#
# Which ids exist on your device:  ttt models --all
#
# The built-ins, for reference — redefine any of them here:
#
#   fast    Qwen/Qwen3-30B-A3B-Instruct
#   smart   Qwen/Qwen3-30B-A3B-Thinking
#   35b     Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B
#   small   Qwen/Qwen3-8B
#   coder   Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B-Instruct
#   tts     Supertone/supertonic-3
#   asr     Qwen/Qwen3-ASR-1.7B
#   embed   Qwen/Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B

# Example: point the everyday aliases at what you actually keep downloaded.
# fast   = Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B-Instruct-Turbo
# smart  = Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B
# vision = Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-turbo
# ocr    = Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-turbo
# music  = tencent/SongGeneration-v2-large

# Aliases are just names — nothing checks them until you load one. A model
# budgeted above the free NPU percentage will evict something; `ttt top` shows
# what is resident and how much of the budget is left.
